The tables of stable real-space invariants (SRSIs) of
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-74844-w, read with no model.

1. srsi_tables(211, spinor=False): one group's tables, end to end
   the tables       : #211.57, 10 SRSIs on 29 site irreps and 17 elementary band
                      representations, 0 symmetry indicators, and 6 splittings of an
                      elementary band representation that the indicators allow
   the SRSI group   : Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z x Z2 x Z2 x Z2
   the basis        : 29 site irreps at Wyckoff positions, 17 of them at maximal ones,
                      17 inducing an elementary band representation
   inducing one     : (A1)_a, (A1)_b, (A1)_c, (A1)_d, (A2)_a, (A2)_b, (A2)_c, (B1)_b,
                      (B1)_d, (B2)_b, (B2)_d, (B3)_d, (E)_a, (E)_b, (E)_c, (T1)_a,
                      (T2)_a
   inducing none    : (1E2E)_e, (1E2E)_f, (A)_e, (A)_g, (A)_h, (A)_i, (A)_j, (A1)_f,
                      (B)_e, (B)_g, (B)_h, (B)_i
   the band count   : nu = 1 theta_1 + 1 theta_2 + 2 theta_3 + 3 theta_4 + 3 theta_5
                      + 3 theta_6 + 4 theta_7
   the band count is itself an SRSI, and bounds the enumeration of atomic realizations

2. two site irreps at one position the invariants do not distinguish
   1 (B2)_d         : Z-valued (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0), mod 2 (0, 0, 1)
   1 (B3)_d         : Z-valued (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0), mod 2 (0, 0, 1)
   the pair         : B2 and B3 at Wyckoff position d, their elementary band
                      representations B2↑G(6) and B3↑G(6)
   both induce the same content at every high-symmetry point and carry the same
   SRSIs, so no measurement in momentum space or in real space tells them apart

3. #147.14, single-valued: printed indicator forms that are not indicators
   the tables       : #147.14, tabulated indicators z2,3 (mod 2), z4 (mod 4)
   1 (Au)_a         : an elementary band representation of #147.14, an atomic limit,
                      so every indicator must read 0 on it
   its SRSIs        : Z-valued (0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
   printed forms    : z2,3 = 1 mod 2, z4 = 2 mod 4
   derived forms    : z2,3 = 0, z4 = 0
   over all systems : 390 tabulated indicator forms against the derived ones:
                      374 equal, 9 with no derived form, 4 different, 3 equivalent
   the different    : #147.14 z2,3, #147.14 z4, #162.74 z2', #163.80 z2'
   where they differ, the indicators returned are the derived forms, which
   vanish on every elementary band representation; the printed forms are kept
   beside them

